  "name": "Midwest FurFest",
  "shortName": "MFF",
  "description": "Midwest FurFest is an annual furry convention in the suburbs of Chicago, Illinois, held since 2000 and run by the non-profit Midwest Furry Fandom, Inc. It began at a hotel in Arlington Heights, moved to Schaumburg in 2002 and to Wheeling in 2008, and has been in Rosemont since 2010, using the Donald E. Stephens Convention Center since 2019. The 2020 edition was held online. Attendance reached 16,925 in 2025. Each year the convention raises money for a chosen charity, with a focus on Chicago-area organisations; its largest total was $185,758 in 2023.",
